    bio: "Ranges from 1B straight to 3A wavy depending on region. Hair is typically dense with thick strands and strong tensile strength. Centuries-old Ayurvedic traditions inform hair care. Hair oiling is a generational practice central to South Asian culture. South Asian men's hair is characterised by high density, thick strand diameter, natural directional wave (2C–3A most common), and jet black pigmentation with strong tensile strength. Scissor-only cuts honour this texture — clipper fades can flatten the density that defines the style.",
